          <startedAt>2026-09-02T00:24:52</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>bfb2f422d6f7df19625dc374c91ab6ec39fbca30</baseCommit>
          <output>Stage 1 (&quot;Create Poem&quot;) completed correctly. Execute rewrote org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.NextPoem.bml with a new, original German poem about a tree and a mushroom (a beech/&quot;Buche&quot; and a &quot;Pilz&quot;), replacing the previous Spanish poem. Supporting fields were updated consistently: &lt;is> now reads &quot;written in German&quot;, the &lt;documentation> body holds the four-stanza German poem, and properties/title changed to &quot;Die Buche und der Pilz&quot;. The author property remains &quot;John Doe&quot;, matching the transformation parameters ({author:&quot;John Doe&quot;,language:&quot;German&quot;}). Only the single playground BML file was modified; no _meta/transform/ ModelTransformation files were touched by Execute. Change is scoped, matches the InstructionTask, and preserves the block's structure and namespaces. Note: Stage 2 (&quot;Translate Poem&quot;) is still pending and will translate this poem to Spanish.</output>
          <completedAt>2026-09-02T00:26:13</completedAt>
          <task>
            <workflow:InstructionTask instructions="Create or update the block org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.NextPoem.bml that contains a random poem in german about a tree and a mushroom. For each execution create a new poem." />
