          <startedAt>2026-09-02T00:26:14</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>e447a8732b02dea25c0604b39fbb8563aaf95361</baseCommit>
          <output>Stage 2 (&quot;Translate Poem&quot;) completed correctly. Execute translated the poem in org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.NextPoem.bml from German to Spanish, matching the InstructionTask. The four-stanza structure and subject matter are preserved: the beech/&quot;Buche&quot; is rendered as &quot;haya&quot; and the mushroom/&quot;Pilz&quot; as &quot;hongo&quot;. Supporting fields were updated consistently: &lt;is> now reads &quot;written in Spanish&quot;, the &lt;documentation> body holds the Spanish translation, and properties/title changed from &quot;Die Buche und der Pilz&quot; to &quot;La haya y el hongo&quot;. The author (&quot;John Doe&quot;) and year (2026) properties are unchanged, and the block's structure, namespaces, type and baseType (core:Documentation) are intact. Only the single playground BML file was modified; no _meta/transform/ ModelTransformation files were touched by Execute. Change is scoped and matches the stage task.</output>
